No.  (Well, I mean, you *can* have those string of words in a sentence, but
it doesn't mean what you think it means ;-) ) BAI (what are confusingly
called "modals" in English) are always pre-positional.  That is, they must
come before the sumti that fills their slot.  (unless, of course, modern
lojbanists have changed the rules on this.  But this is CLL lojban)

             --gejyspa

